---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Container from '../../components/ui/Container.astro';
import SectionBar from '../../components/ui/SectionBar.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="China Market Entry via Social Commerce | TheRedScroll"
  description="Enter the market through social commerce. Account setup, brand localization, Douyin Shop, WeChat Mini Programs. Team on the ground in Shanghai."
>

  <!-- Hero — Dark hero banner -->
  <section class="relative w-full overflow-hidden bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
    <div class="relative z-[1] max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-[48px] max-[1024px]:px-[32px] max-[640px]:px-[20px] pt-[160px] pb-[96px] max-[640px]:pt-[112px] max-[640px]:pb-[56px] text-center">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[#CC3333] mb-[16px]">
        China market entry support
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-[#FFFFFF] text-[48px] max-[640px]:text-[28px] font-medium leading-[1.15] mb-[16px]">
        Listing your product isn't enough. If nobody knows you exist, nobody buys.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.7)] text-[18px] max-[640px]:text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.5] mb-[40px]">
        Enter the market through social media. Faster, cheaper, and more testable than a traditional marketplace launch.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-[12px] flex-wrap">
        <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Book a call</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary-dark" href="#what-we-do">See what we do</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why social media comes first -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[48px] max-[640px]:gap-[32px] items-start">
        <div>
          <SectionBar />
          <SectionHeading overline="The problem">Most brands start in the wrong place.</SectionHeading>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
            <p>
              Most brands think market entry starts with getting listed on Tmall or JD. Set up a store, upload your products, wait for orders. Five years ago that could work. It really can't anymore.
            </p>
            <p>
              What happens in practice: you launch a Tmall Global store. Products go live. But nobody searches for your brand because nobody has heard of it. Zero reviews. Zero social proof.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col pt-[48px] max-[640px]:pt-[0px]">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
            <p>
              Consumers check RedNote before they buy. They search Douyin for demos. They look for your WeChat. They find nothing. They buy from a brand that shows up.
            </p>
            <p>
              That's why social media should be the first step. Not something you bolt on after the marketplace store is already struggling. People need to know your brand exists before you invest in a Tmall flagship or a JD cross-border operation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Social commerce changes the equation — dark section -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="bg-[#1A1A1A] rounded-[12px] p-[48px] max-[640px]:p-[32px_20px]">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[8px]">Social commerce</p>
        <h2 class="text-[#FFFFFF] text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.25] mb-[16px]">Social platforms aren't just awareness channels anymore. They sell product.</h2>
        <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5] max-w-[680px] mb-[32px]">
          You can enter the market through social commerce first. Test products, build a following, collect actual sales data, and prove there's demand before taking on the cost and complexity of a full marketplace operation.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[24px]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">Douyin</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              RMB 3.5 trillion in e-commerce sales in 2024. Users find a product in a video, tap a link, buy without leaving the app. Third-largest e-commerce channel by transaction volume.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">RedNote</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              Supports in-app purchases, brand stores, and livestream shopping. A consumer can go from reading a KOC (Key Opinion Consumer) review to checkout in under 30 seconds.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">WeChat Mini Programs</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              Full e-commerce stores inside WeChat. Product catalog, payment, order tracking, loyalty. Active Mini Shop merchants doubled in 2024, total GMV up 200% year on year.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- It's cheaper to start on social -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[48px] max-[640px]:p-[32px_20px]">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[24px] text-center">Cost comparison</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[32px] max-[640px]:gap-[24px] text-center">
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">¥100,000+</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Tmall Global setup: deposit fees, annual charges, store design, and minimum ad spend before you've sold anything.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[4px]">¥15,000 to ¥30,000/mo</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Social-first entry: account setup, content production, and KOC seeding. Testing product-market fit with real people giving real feedback.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-[680px] mx-auto mt-[32px]">
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)] text-center">
            Doesn't mean you should forget about marketplaces. Just means social should come first. It builds the awareness and trust that marketplace sales end up depending on.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- What we do -->
  <section id="what-we-do" class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px] scroll-mt-[76px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="What we do">Market research and account setup</SectionHeading>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[48px] max-[640px]:gap-[32px] items-start">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)] max-w-[680px]">
          <p>
            Before anything else, we study your category. Who's selling similar products. What platforms they use. What content they post. How they price things. Where the openings are, if there are any.
          </p>
          <p>
            We pull competitor social accounts across RedNote, Douyin, WeChat, and Weibo. Content themes, posting frequency, engagement rates, KOL (Key Opinion Leader) partnerships, ad activity. All of it. You get a clear picture of what you're walking into before a single yuan gets spent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Account setup and verification</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)] mb-[24px]">
            We register and verify your brand accounts on all relevant platforms. WeChat Official Account, RedNote Business Account, Douyin Business Account, Weibo Blue V. Each platform has its own verification process, documentation, and timelines. The whole process is managed by our team so you're not stuck on Chinese-language admin portals.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Brand localization</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">
            Chinese brand naming, visual identity adaptation, packaging guidance, and messaging frameworks for each platform. Trademark registration in China typically takes 9 to 12 months, so we start that process early while the social launch moves forward in parallel.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Social commerce integration — cards -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Commerce">Social commerce integration</SectionHeading>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px] mt-[24px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Douyin Shop</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Cross-border sales without a domestic entity. Products link to short videos and live streams, cutting the gap between discovery and purchase to almost nothing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">WeChat Mini Program stores</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Your own storefront inside WeChat. Cross-border payment, product catalog, order management. Connected to your Official Account and distributable through articles, ads, and QR codes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">RedNote in-app stores</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Product listings linked directly to your notes and KOL content. Ideal for brands in beauty, lifestyle, and fashion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Cross-border logistics</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Bonded warehouses and cross-border logistics providers handle fulfillment. No local entity or local inventory needed to get started. We connect you with the right partners based on your product category and shipping volumes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Launch strategy -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="max-w-[680px]">
        <SectionBar />
        <SectionHeading overline="Execution">Launch strategy and execution</SectionHeading>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          <p>
            We build a 90-day launch plan. Platform selection, content strategy, KOC seeding roadmap, ad budget allocation, milestone KPIs.
          </p>
          <p>
            Then we run it. Content production, account management, influencer coordination, ad campaigns, weekly reporting. Everything that needs to happen in the first three months to go from nothing to something real.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Case study -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[48px] max-[640px]:p-[32px_20px]">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[8px]">Case study</p>
        <h2 class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.25] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[24px]">Italian premium olive oil brand enters through social commerce</h2>

        <div class="max-w-[680px] flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          <p>
            An Italian premium olive oil brand wanted to test the market before committing to a Tmall store. Strong distribution across Europe but zero recognition among Chinese consumers. Budget was limited to roughly $8,000/month for the first three months.
          </p>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-stone)]">
            The brand's first idea was a Tmall Global store. But the setup costs, store design, listing fees, and minimum ad spend needed to compete would have consumed the entire first-year budget. With no guarantee anyone would actually find the store.
          </p>
          <p>
            We recommended a social-first launch. Month one: research and setup. Registered accounts on RedNote and WeChat. Studied the premium cooking oil category on RedNote and found almost nobody was doing educational content about olive oil varietals, origins, or cooking applications. That gap became the entire content strategy.
          </p>
          <p>
            Month two: 12 RedNote notes focused on cooking education, recipes, and Italian origin stories. Product sent to 25 micro-KOCs in the food space. A WeChat article series on Mediterranean cooking launched alongside a Mini Program store with cross-border shipping.
          </p>
          <p>
            Month three: boosted top RedNote notes with Juguang ads. Brought in two mid-tier food KOLs for sponsored recipe videos. Mini Program store went live with three hero SKUs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Results grid -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-4 max-[640px]:grid-cols-2 gap-[24px] mt-[32px] pt-[32px] border-t border-[rgba(0,0,0,0.08)]">
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">25</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">KOC reviews indexed on RedNote for olive oil and Italian cooking oil searches.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">4,200</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">RedNote followers from zero.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[4px]">¥38,000</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">WeChat Mini Program store direct sales. No marketplace commissions.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">+40%</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Average order value versus the brand's European online average.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Callout -->
        <div class="bg-white border-l-[3px] border-[#CC3333] rounded-none p-[20px] mt-[32px]">
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal text-[#1A1A1A] leading-[1.6] m-0">
            The brand postponed Tmall and committed to 12 months of social-first distribution. Social commerce let them test real demand at a fraction of what a Tmall launch would have cost.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- How to get started -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Get started">Ready to enter the market?</SectionHeading>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px] mt-[24px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">01</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Book a 30-minute discovery call</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">We learn about your brand, product, and goals.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">02</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Get a market entry proposal</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Platform recommendations, launch timeline, and fixed pricing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">03</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Account setup and first content</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Initial sales within 60 to 90 days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="FAQ">Frequently asked questions</SectionHeading>

      <div class="max-w-[680px] flex flex-col gap-[32px] mt-[24px]">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Do we need a local entity to start selling?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">No. Cross-border e-commerce lets you sell through Douyin Shop, WeChat Mini Programs, and RedNote stores without setting up a domestic company. You will need a Hong Kong or overseas business license and a logistics partner with bonded warehouse access. We help get all of that in place.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How much budget do we need?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">A social-first entry can start from ¥15,000 to ¥30,000/month covering account setup, content production, and KOC seeding. Add ¥10,000 to ¥20,000/month for advertising if you want to move faster. Compare that to Tmall Global which typically requires ¥100,000+ in setup and deposit fees before you've sold anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Should we skip Tmall and JD entirely?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">No, not forever. Both platforms are powerful once you have recognition and steady demand. But launching there first, without a social presence backing you up, usually ends with high spend and low return. Build awareness through social channels, then expand to marketplaces when the numbers support it.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How long until we see sales?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">If you're selling through Douyin Shop or a WeChat Mini Program, first orders can come in within 30 to 60 days. Repeatable volume usually takes 90 to 120 days as the content library and review base fill out.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">What categories work best for social-first entry?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Beauty, skincare, health supplements, food and beverage, fashion, lifestyle. Anything visual, reviewable, and story-friendly tends to gain traction fastest on RedNote and Douyin. B2B and industrial products take a different route, usually WeChat and Zhihu. Some categories like cosmetics, food, and health supplements face import registration requirements that can add 3 to 6 months to the timeline. We flag those early.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Can you help with product registration and compliance?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">We cover the social media and commerce side. For product registration (CFDA for cosmetics, health product approvals, food import licenses), we work with compliance partners who specialize in that. We coordinate the process and tell you upfront what's required for your category.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">What if our product already sells on Tmall but isn't performing?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Usually the issue isn't the listing itself. It's the lack of social presence driving traffic to it. We audit your situation and typically recommend adding a social layer: RedNote reviews, Douyin content, WeChat CRM. Marketplace numbers tend to improve once people can find your brand outside the marketplace.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Do you handle logistics and shipping?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Not directly. We work with established cross-border logistics providers and bonded warehouse operators. We take care of the platform and commerce setup. They take care of fulfillment. And we coordinate between the two so you're not juggling separate vendor relationships on your own.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How do consumers discover new foreign brands?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Social media, overwhelmingly. Data from 2025 shows 42% of younger consumers search Douyin first when looking for products, 30% go to RedNote, and only 17% start on Baidu. Discovery happens inside social apps now, not on search engines.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Can we sell in RMB if we're based overseas?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Yes, that's all handled by the platforms. Consumers pay in RMB. You get paid in your local currency through the platform settlement process. Both WeChat Mini Programs and Douyin Shop support this.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px] mb-[0px]">
    <div class="w-full bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] py-[64px] max-[640px]:py-[48px] px-[48px] max-[640px]:px-[20px]">
      <div class="max-w-[600px] mx-auto text-center">
        <h2 class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.25] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">
          Ready to enter the market?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[14px] text-[var(--color-stone)] font-normal leading-[1.6] mb-[24px]">
          30-minute discovery call. Market entry proposal with fixed pricing. Account setup and first content within 60 to 90 days.
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-[12px] flex-wrap">
          <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Book a call</Button>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/pricing">See pricing</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</PageLayout>
